} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f38aa5a6-726f-571b-8466-b09c1fec5790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345109} {:answer/id #uuid "b39387df-8446-5f45-992e-91240d987093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ne " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345110} {:answer/id #uuid "6b2344bc-fffa-5d35-ac5b-20e04e8932b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345111} {:answer/id #uuid "283eff25-f8ee-5d8f-9485-ea83094447fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345112} {:answer/id #uuid "d471d7c8-202e-5bc1-a13e-9da3478c70f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d471d7c8-202e-5bc1-a13e-9da3478c70f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345113} :answer-field/id #uuid "37805294-8b4c-59af-9bba-9e6d3aadc83e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f12574d2-ca01-52cd-b44a-2021e52b83d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181687" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063256/assets/f6a3b3bc0064525271804e6d20689c21ca84c0adad138a8bd8d398be66e45c3e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,-x-1\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,x+2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=-x-1$ and *below* the line $y=x+2.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>-x-1,\\,y<x+2.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n-x-1<y<x+2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-x-1<y<x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362" :knowledge-point/title "Linear Boundaries, Two Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbdc19b-0e30-5a57-be12-31a21bcaf24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345116} {:answer/id #uuid "1df22536-bccf-5f00-981d-d8acbd44a103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345117} {:answer/id #uuid "3c35a65b-912e-5d65-bef9-d04c33c9a45f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345118} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcd0c25-68a7-5573-b5d7-087afeda1df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345119} {:answer/id #uuid "af35d99a-a8da-5895-9505-3863f21e4713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbdc19b-0e30-5a57-be12-31a21bcaf24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345116} :answer-field/id #uuid "edefcb13-ba5f-5ef0-b2c2-ff7a424102c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f969d7c3-8ac6-514c-87b6-c5f2645c2e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345122} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c83159-fd7e-5564-887b-be3872686bff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\